    "assistant_text": "The per-line-item summary confirms the earlier hypothesis: discounting each line separately and summing accumulates rounding differently than discounting the subtotal once. Computing it by hand \u2014 per-item discount sums to 105.66, but discount on the subtotal is 105.67, a one-cent difference that exactly matches the test's expected total of 1324.83. Fixing `settle()` to discount the subtotal directly.\nAll 6 tests pass. The bug was in `engine.py:46-48` \u2014 `settle()` applied the promotional discount per line item and summed the roundings, instead of applying it once to the invoice subtotal. That accumulated an extra half-cent of rounding (105.66 vs the correct 105.67), making total_due 1324.84 instead of 1324.83 and causing the exact-payment test to report `UNDERPAID`. Replaced the per-item loop with a single `rules.discount_for(subtotal)` call.",
